# Solidity dependencies are materialised by `make deps` from harness/deps.lock,
# not committed. The lockfile pins exact commits, so this is reproducible without
# carrying 62 MB of other people's history in our tree.
harness/lib/
corpus/lib

# Upstream checkouts used for reading ground truth during development.
.vendor/

# Foundry
out/
cache/
broadcast/
*.gcda

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
# Build artefact of packaging the detectors: setuptools copies
# errors/catalog.json in here so an installed wheel carries the catalogue. The
# canonical file is the one under errors/; a copy in the tree would drift.
detectors/slither_hookrisk/data/

# hookrisk output
hook-risk.json
hook-risk.invalid.json
HOOK_RISK.md
hookrisk.sarif
hookrisk-debug/
.hookrisk-cache/

# ...except under docs/hackathon/evidence, where those same filenames are the
# point: they are the recorded before/after of scanning 14 real hooks, and the
# claims in the write-up are only checkable against them. The patterns above are
# filename-shaped, so every one of those manifests matched and had to be
# `git add -f`ed, which is exactly how a piece of evidence goes missing.
#
# The negation works because no *directory* on the path is excluded — git cannot
# re-include a file underneath an excluded directory, so this would silently do
# nothing if `docs/` or `evidence/` were ever ignored.
!docs/hackathon/evidence/**

# Local environment
.env
.env.local

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
